{
  "name": "Unarmed Fighting",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>(Prerequisite: Fighting Style Feature)</em></p><p>When you hit with your Unarmed Strike and deal damage, you can deal Bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 plus your Strength modifier instead of the normal damage of an Unarmed Strike. If you aren’t holding any weapons or a Shield when you make the attack roll, the d6 becomes a d8.</p><p>At the start of each of your turns, you can deal 1d4 Bludgeoning damage to one creature &amp;Reference[Grappled] by you.</p><section id=\"secret-Nv8dMOvrI9GVk4P5\" class=\"secret\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The <strong>Unarmed Strike (Weapon in Hand)</strong> activity can be used in place of your normal Unarmed Strike.</p><p>The <strong>Unarmed Strike (Empty Hand)</strong> activity includes the increased damage.</p><p>The <strong>Grappled Damage</strong> activity includes the damage roll.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
